       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Sertraline 600 mg daily is three times the maximum labeled adult dose of 200 mg/day. At that dose the risks include serotonin syndrome, seizures, QT prolongation, and GI or bleeding effects. Your patient has normal renal and hepatic function and no listed allergies, so nothing here would justify going above the maximum.\n\nCould this be a typo? Usual dosing is:\n- **Starting dose:** 25\u201350 mg once daily\n- **Usual range:** 50\u2013200 mg once daily\n\nPlease tell me which of these you want:\n1. **A corrected dose.** Give me the dose, such as 50, 100, or 200 mg PO daily, and I'll enter it right away.\n2. **600 mg as written.** If that's intentional, for example under a specialist's direction, tell me and add a rationale for the order note. I'd suggest pharmacy verification as well."
